{
  "realm": "itsm",
  "displayName": "IT Service Management",
  "enabled": true,
  "sslRequired": "all",
  "registrationAllowed": false,
  "loginWithEmailAllowed": true,
  "duplicateEmailsAllowed": false,
  "resetPasswordAllowed": true,
  "editUsernameAllowed": false,
  "bruteForceProtected": true,
  "permanentLockout": false,
  "maxFailureWaitSeconds": 900,
  "failureFactor": 10,
  "accessTokenLifespan": 300,
  "ssoSessionIdleTimeout": 1800,
  "ssoSessionMaxLifespan": 36000,
  "offlineSessionIdleTimeout": 2592000,
  "attributes": {
    "frontendUrl": "",
    "comment.frontendUrl": "Set per environment by the deploy workflow to https://auth.<environment-label>.<domain>. Left empty here because a realm file with one environment's hostname baked in is a realm file that is wrong in the other two."
  },

  "comment.userProfile": [
    "tenant_id is a declared user attribute, not an ad-hoc one.",
    "apps/api/src/auth/verify.ts refuses any token whose payload has no tenant_id:",
    "'this token names no tenant'. So the attribute, the mapper below that copies",
    "it into the access token, and SCIM writing it at provisioning time are three",
    "halves of one mechanism — break any and every sign-in fails closed, which is",
    "the right direction but an expensive way to learn the claim was missing.",
    "itsm_user_id is optional: verify.ts falls back to `sub` when it is absent."
  ],
  "userProfile": {
    "attributes": [
      { "name": "username", "displayName": "${username}", "permissions": { "view": ["admin", "user"], "edit": ["admin"] } },
      { "name": "email", "displayName": "${email}", "required": { "roles": ["user"] }, "permissions": { "view": ["admin", "user"], "edit": ["admin", "user"] } },
      { "name": "firstName", "displayName": "${firstName}", "required": { "roles": ["user"] }, "permissions": { "view": ["admin", "user"], "edit": ["admin", "user"] } },
      { "name": "lastName", "displayName": "${lastName}", "required": { "roles": ["user"] }, "permissions": { "view": ["admin", "user"], "edit": ["admin", "user"] } },
      {
        "name": "tenant_id",
        "displayName": "Tenant",
        "required": { "roles": ["user"] },
        "permissions": { "view": ["admin", "user"], "edit": ["admin"] },
        "validations": { "length": { "min": 1, "max": 64 } }
      },
      {
        "name": "itsm_user_id",
        "displayName": "ITSM user id",
        "permissions": { "view": ["admin", "user"], "edit": ["admin"] },
        "validations": { "length": { "min": 0, "max": 64 } }
      }
    ]
  },

  "comment.clientScopes": [
    "One shared scope carries the two claims the API reads, rather than four",
    "copies of the same two mappers on four clients. A mapper that exists on",
    "three clients out of four is the kind of fault that looks like 'only the",
    "console is broken'."
  ],
  "clientScopes": [
    {
      "name": "itsm-claims",
      "description": "The tenant and user claims apps/api reads off every access token",
      "protocol": "openid-connect",
      "attributes": { "include.in.token.scope": "true", "display.on.consent.screen": "false" },
      "protocolMappers": [
        {
          "name": "tenant-id",
          "protocol": "openid-connect",
          "protocolMapper": "oidc-usermodel-attribute-mapper",
          "consentRequired": false,
          "config": {
            "user.attribute": "tenant_id",
            "claim.name": "tenant_id",
            "jsonType.label": "String",
            "id.token.claim": "true",
            "access.token.claim": "true",
            "userinfo.token.claim": "true"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "itsm-user-id",
          "protocol": "openid-connect",
          "protocolMapper": "oidc-usermodel-attribute-mapper",
          "consentRequired": false,
          "config": {
            "user.attribute": "itsm_user_id",
            "claim.name": "itsm_user_id",
            "jsonType.label": "String",
            "id.token.claim": "true",
            "access.token.claim": "true",
            "userinfo.token.claim": "true"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "audience-itsm-api",
          "protocol": "openid-connect",
          "protocolMapper": "oidc-audience-mapper",
          "consentRequired": false,
          "config": {
            "comment": "Without this the access token's aud names the front-end client, and jwtVerify refuses it against OIDC_AUDIENCE=itsm-api. Nothing else in the token would look wrong.",
            "included.client.audience": "itsm-api",
            "id.token.claim": "false",
            "access.token.claim": "true"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "defaultDefaultClientScopes": ["itsm-claims"],

  "comment.clients": [
    "Three confidential clients, one per application, and one bearer-only",
    "resource server. Separate rather than shared because the redirect URI is",
    "what stops an authorisation code being returned to somewhere else, and one",
    "client holding all three origins' URIs is one compromised application away",
    "from being all of them.",
    "",
    "redirectUris and webOrigins are placeholders resolved per environment by",
    "the deploy workflow from DEPLOY_DOMAIN. The + in webOrigins means 'the",
    "origins of the redirect URIs', so it needs no substitution."
  ],
  "clients": [
    {
      "clientId": "itsm-api",
      "name": "ITSM API",
      "description": "The resource server. Issues nothing; every token is addressed to it.",
      "enabled": true,
      "protocol": "openid-connect",
      "bearerOnly": true,
      "publicClient": false,
      "standardFlowEnabled": false,
      "directAccessGrantsEnabled": false,
      "serviceAccountsEnabled": false
    },
    {
      "clientId": "itsm-portal",
      "name": "Requester portal",
      "enabled": true,
      "protocol": "openid-connect",
      "publicClient": false,
      "standardFlowEnabled": true,
      "implicitFlowEnabled": false,
      "directAccessGrantsEnabled": false,
      "serviceAccountsEnabled": false,
      "attributes": { "pkce.code.challenge.method": "S256", "post.logout.redirect.uris": "https://help.__DOMAIN__/*" },
      "redirectUris": ["https://help.__DOMAIN__/api/session/callback"],
      "webOrigins": ["+"],
      "defaultClientScopes": ["openid", "profile", "email", "itsm-claims"]
    },
    {
      "clientId": "itsm-workbench",
      "name": "Agent workbench",
      "enabled": true,
      "protocol": "openid-connect",
      "publicClient": false,
      "standardFlowEnabled": true,
      "implicitFlowEnabled": false,
      "directAccessGrantsEnabled": false,
      "serviceAccountsEnabled": false,
      "attributes": { "pkce.code.challenge.method": "S256", "post.logout.redirect.uris": "https://desk.__DOMAIN__/*" },
      "redirectUris": ["https://desk.__DOMAIN__/api/session/callback"],
      "webOrigins": ["+"],
      "defaultClientScopes": ["openid", "profile", "email", "itsm-claims"]
    },
    {
      "clientId": "itsm-admin",
      "name": "Administration console",
      "description": "Separate from the workbench so an agent session is not also a console session.",
      "enabled": true,
      "protocol": "openid-connect",
      "publicClient": false,
      "standardFlowEnabled": true,
      "implicitFlowEnabled": false,
      "directAccessGrantsEnabled": false,
      "serviceAccountsEnabled": false,
      "attributes": { "pkce.code.challenge.method": "S256", "post.logout.redirect.uris": "https://admin.__DOMAIN__/*" },
      "redirectUris": ["https://admin.__DOMAIN__/api/session/callback"],
      "webOrigins": ["+"],
      "defaultClientScopes": ["openid", "profile", "email", "itsm-claims"]
    }
  ]
}
